{
  "abstract": "For every finite simple graph and k ≥ 0, the signed evaluation (−1)^n χ_G(−k) counts acyclic orientations paired with weakly compatible Fin k colorings (Stanley 1973, Theorem 1.2); at k = 1 it counts acyclic orientations (Corollary 1.3). Includes positive-evaluation correctness, induced-subgraph convolution, and the finite equivalence between well-foundedness and no directed cycles.",
